  "id": "thin-stripes",
  "term": "thin stripes",
  "definition": "Thin stripes are subdivisions of visual cortical area V2 involved in surface-based processing within the V1 blob–V2 thin stripe–V4 pathway. In the source model, surface representations in V2 thin stripes send feedback that helps boundary representations support figure-ground separation and the conscious perception of 3D surfaces.",
